Senior Consultant, Data Science 

 

Company Description:

Moviri Consulting is the first company of Moviri and its foundation. Moviri’s professionals use data, software, and insights to solve substantial business challenges for Fortune 500 corporations, multinational banks, global media conglomerates and some of the most respected brands in a variety of industries. The Moviri Consulting Analytics team revolutionizes enterprise processes and customer relations, thanks to data science and big data processing.

 

Job Description:

A Senior Consultant is an AI and ML expert that knows how to implement, develop and deliver advanced models and machine learning solutions in Big Data environments. You will have the ownership to manage different cross-industry customer projects in the field of Data Science.  

Full-time position at the Milan/Padova Office.

 

Responsibilities:

Act as a SME in the pre-sales process;
Be the owner of the ML/AI projects 
Help translate project goals in project activities;
Drive a related effort estimation;
Be a ML technical focal point in the execution of one or more projects.

 

Job Requirements:

Master’s Degree in Computer Science, Data Science and Engineering, Statistic or similar;
5 years of professional experience in Data Science 
Confidence with ML frameworks and libraries like PyTorch, Tensorflow, Numpy, Keras;
Knowledge of modeling tools e.g. AWS Sagemaker, GCP Vertex AI, Kubeflow, MLflow, RAY;
Strong statistical knowledge;
Preferred experience with time series forecasting, anomaly detection or computer vision;
Ability to switch between different technologies and tools;
Fluent in English. Good Italian.

 

What we look for:

Passion. Staying ahead of the curve, solving tough problems. That’s hard to do without a genuine passion for technology and conviction in your ideas. 

Curiosity. We aim to solve hard business problems, using the latest technology and research. Curiosity is key in providing a fresh perspective and generating new approaches. 

Drive. You will be asked to drive complex tasks from start to finish and carry your colleagues along, sometimes in areas where you have limited experience. 

Humbleness. No one is right 100% of the time. While we have internationally-recognized experts on our team, we like to stay humble, listen and learn.

 

What we offer:

Outstanding peers. We hire some of the most talented graduates from top universities and recognized industry experts with an impressive professional track record.

Professional growth. We offer technical and managerial growth paths across our group’s companies and promote based on performance, regardless of age or seniority.

Global opportunities. We are a global multinational, with offices in Italy, United States and Singapore and customers in 45+ countries across the world. 

Startup environment. With over 200 people and a 20-year history, we combine the youthfulness and agility of a startup with the solidity of an established company.

Cool workplace. We invest in dynamic working spaces, productivity software and digital tools to collaborate, share ideas and get things done.

 

Compensation & Benefits:

Competitive salary package;
Yearly performance bonus;
Per-diem allowance for out of office assignments;
Meal vouchers;
Welfare program to pay for public transportation, cinemas, gym, Amazon vouchers and more;
Integrative health insurance;
Lenovo or MacBook Pro laptop and latest generation smartphone;
Continuous learning and training: O’Reilly Safari library, professional certifications, meetups, conferences & tradeshows;
Terrace beer happy hour every Friday;
Annual offsite company meeting.
